[Work Order TK-20260920-7580 · Creator Appeal Review · Full description]
Submitter: Operations Supervisor of a Chain Store (Account Ending 4471)
Content involved: Comment posted on 2026-10-17 02:11. The original text "This supplier's frozen product purchase price rose 18% this quarter, and our S-739 has already been replaced," was deemed "false information," deleted and restricted for 7 days.
Main Text of Appeal: I have submitted a procurement price comparison table. The average price in Q3 2022 was 21.4 yuan/kg, and in Q4 it was 25.3 yuan/kg, an increase of exactly 18.2%. Please read carefully before making a judgment.
Review process:
1. Verify the appeal attachment "B-45482 Batch Price Comparison Table," which states the statistical period from Q3 2022 to Q4 2022, which is two years different from the "quarter" mentioned in the comment;
2. Reviewing the same supplier's Q2 and Q3 2024 quotation records on the platform, both periods were 25.3 yuan/kg, a 0% quarter-on-quarter change. The comment saying "18% increase" had no corresponding data for that period;
3. The appellant added a message at 09:39 on 2026-09-05 stating "The form may have been taken by mistake," and no new evidence was submitted as of the review date;
4. Unrelated item: This account has another appeal TK-20260902-5960 related to image watermark issues, which has been transferred separately.
Conclusion: The counter-evidence materials do not correspond to the time period involved, and the current quotation did not increase. Confidence: Very high.

[On-site appeals · CS-007323】
Appeal Body: You say I violated regulations by "disclosing partner business names," but I have read Article 3.2 of the current "Community Content Specification" verbatim and only prohibit disclosure of "undisclosed quotations and contract amounts," not mentioning business names. In my comments, there is only a description of the "East China region of a certain supply chain company," with no price figures at all. Please re-determine according to the current terms.
Review Records:
- Retrieve the current version: Clause 3.2 (revised 2026-09-13) states "No disclosure of partners' undisclosed quotations, contract amounts, or rebate rates," and business names are not included;
- Full text of the comment involved: "A certain supply chain company in East China has sent another letter saying they want to renegotiate the annual framework, and that our 32 stores will be executed at original prices for now." The text contains no amount, no quotation, and no rebate rate;
- The "Clause 3.2 (including trade names)" cited in the original judgment was the old version before the amendment, which became invalid on the revision date;
- Unrelated: The image copyright appeal for TK-20261011-0532 is still pending.
Processing: Revoke deletion and limit usage. Accuracy: Very high (clause versions and commentary texts are matched item by item).

